# Test: REST users come from zefs and system.authentication independently of SSH,
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
#       keep strict AAA profiles, and follow live reloads.
# VALIDATES: AC-1, AC-2, AC-6, and AC-12 of
#            spec-hub-deferred-api-auth-independent-of-ssh-block.
# PREVENTS: API authentication and no-BGP AAA depending on environment.ssh,
#           config collisions retaining zefs credentials or recovery authority,
#           rebuilt authenticators reviving removed users, and authorization
#           profiles remaining pinned to the boot store after reload.
#
# One config-only boot proves AC-1 and AC-2 with no zefs database. Two further
# boots discriminate the zefs/config producer in runYANGConfig: distinct names,
# then a collision followed by boot-built and reload-built authenticator checks.
# None of the configs contains BGP or SSH.

option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture ui/api-user-removed-by-reload:timeout=120s
expect=exit:code=0
